# Terraform working state (never commit)
.terraform/
.terraform.lock.hcl
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfvars
crash.log

# Ignoring .terraform.lock.hcl is a deliberate deviation from HashiCorp's style guide (which
# says to commit it): these modules are throwaway compatibility probes, so a fresh checkout
# resolves the current unmodified provider within `~> 3.0` instead of a pinned patch release.
# A local lockfile still pins subsequent runs in the same directory until it is deleted (the
# runbooks' teardown does) or `terraform init -upgrade` is used. The version actually tested
# is recorded in docs/compatibility/TERRAFORM_COMPATIBILITY_REPORT.md.
